1
00:00:14,120 --> 00:00:18,420
Aiming for the setting sun
floating over the Nakagawa,

2
00:00:18,420 --> 00:00:23,580
I kicked a pebble,
sending it flying as far as it would go.

3
00:00:24,140 --> 00:00:29,400
Talking away to the head of the gym class,

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:33,820
I got laughed at for
staying so full of energy.

5
00:00:33,820 --> 00:00:37,440
Even if I stir up some
good spirit somewhere,

6
00:00:37,440 --> 00:00:38,680
there's only winning,
there's a reason for it.

7
00:00:38,680 --> 00:00:41,940
A nightmare,
one street scene that never changes,

8
00:00:41,940 --> 00:00:43,880
is gentler than before.

9
00:00:44,560 --> 00:00:46,860
Because the crows are cawing,

10
00:00:46,860 --> 00:00:48,700
the sun has already gone down.

11
00:00:49,800 --> 00:00:51,940
Stuffing yakitori in my mouth,

12
00:00:51,940 --> 00:00:53,840
even just looking at it...

13
00:00:54,660 --> 00:00:57,500
of the little acorn cap,

14
00:00:57,500 --> 00:01:04,060
from the waterworks,
the big power lines and the sunset fall.

15
00:01:06,740 --> 00:01:10,100
Tomorrow too,
it'll end with it dropping away, won't it?

16
00:01:10,100 --> 00:01:13,660
Katsushika,
for a while even happiness is lost.

17
00:01:13,660 --> 00:01:16,300
Because I've only just realized,
I'm the one who...

18
00:01:24,780 --> 00:01:27,020
The tuna-riding police officer

19
00:01:31,940 --> 00:01:32,960
Come on, everyone.

20
00:01:33,860 --> 00:01:35,860
Today's going to be a bit busy, so

21
00:01:35,860 --> 00:01:38,120
hurry up and eat your lunch, will you?

22
00:01:38,620 --> 00:01:39,000
Yes.

23
00:01:39,640 --> 00:01:40,640
Hey, Gepard.

24
00:01:40,640 --> 00:01:42,400
I want sushi, okay?

25
00:01:42,400 --> 00:01:44,760
Then make whatever you
like yourself and eat it.

26
00:01:45,260 --> 00:01:45,640
Go on, do it.

27
00:01:46,300 --> 00:01:48,900
This is why I can't quit
my sushi shop part-time job!

28
00:01:48,900 --> 00:01:49,720
Fatty tuna.

29
00:01:49,720 --> 00:01:51,740
Yeah, that's prime fatty tuna.

30
00:01:52,880 --> 00:01:54,220
No fatty tuna for me!

31
00:01:54,360 --> 00:01:55,820
Ugh, just as I thought.

32
00:01:56,340 --> 00:01:58,495
I've been meaning to
ask you this for a while,

33
00:01:58,545 --> 00:02:01,340
why is the fatty tuna always in-house?

34
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:05,294
Well, the fatty part is only
a small portion of a whole tuna,

35
00:02:05,344 --> 00:02:06,300
so it's precious.

36
00:02:07,100 --> 00:02:10,500
Besides,
we only use tuna caught in nearby waters,

37
00:02:11,060 --> 00:02:13,840
and bluefin tuna itself is
getting scarcer every year.

38
00:02:14,680 --> 00:02:15,400
I see.

39
00:02:16,300 --> 00:02:18,960
But if customers don't know the prices,
they'll be scared off.

40
00:02:19,300 --> 00:02:22,880
Prices are set by the market,
so there's nothing we can do.

41
00:02:24,720 --> 00:02:27,480
I smell it. I smell money.

42
00:02:32,180 --> 00:02:33,740
It's Ikkyu-san

43
00:02:34,220 --> 00:02:37,820
To make it cheaper, you just need to
cut back on the middleman's margin.

44
00:02:38,080 --> 00:02:40,880
Wholesalers, retailers, and so on take
a lot of work, so it ends up expensive.

45
00:02:40,880 --> 00:02:45,540
If the sushi shop went and got the fish directly,
it could serve it cheaply and consistently.

46
00:02:45,540 --> 00:02:48,260
That's true, but it's impossible, isn't it?

47
00:02:48,260 --> 00:02:49,780
No, it's doable.

48
00:02:49,780 --> 00:02:53,780
I'm pretty sure Kanbei has a
friend who catches tuna in Aomori.

49
00:02:54,220 --> 00:02:55,500
I'll go catch some right away.

50
00:02:55,500 --> 00:02:56,120
Hey, wait.

51
00:02:57,820 --> 00:02:59,160
He's already gone.

52
00:03:00,180 --> 00:03:02,300
That's just the kind of
idea he'd come up with.

53
00:03:13,860 --> 00:03:14,780
Excuse me.

54
00:03:14,780 --> 00:03:17,920
Which one is the boat of Gen-san,
the tuna-fishing master?

55
00:03:17,920 --> 00:03:18,900
Gen-san.

56
00:03:19,620 --> 00:03:21,420
Santiago-san?

57
00:03:21,420 --> 00:03:24,460
If it's Santiago-san's boat,
it's the one at the very back.

58
00:03:24,460 --> 00:03:25,360
Santiago.

59
00:03:30,840 --> 00:03:32,760
So this is Gen-san's boat?

60
00:03:32,760 --> 00:03:35,560
Hemingu Ichigo.

61
00:03:36,420 --> 00:03:38,640
What's with this weird boat name?

62
00:03:38,640 --> 00:03:40,740
The last part is read as "way."

63
00:03:42,400 --> 00:03:44,420
So it's Hemingway-language, then.

64
00:03:44,960 --> 00:03:46,960
It sounds like a biker gang's name.

65
00:03:47,460 --> 00:03:48,820
That old man, is he Gen-san?

66
00:03:48,820 --> 00:03:51,920
Isn't he Gen-san?

67
00:03:54,640 --> 00:03:55,620
W-what?

68
00:03:56,080 --> 00:03:57,900
Don't just call him Santiago.
Call him Captain Santiago!

69
00:03:59,920 --> 00:04:00,740
Wh-why?

70
00:04:01,480 --> 00:04:04,520
Speaking of Hemingway,
it's The Old Man and the Sea, right?

71
00:04:04,920 --> 00:04:06,600
I don't know anything about that.

72
00:04:07,200 --> 00:04:09,500
You don't even know such a famous novel?

73
00:04:09,500 --> 00:04:12,680
The protagonist of this
novel is named Santiago.

74
00:04:12,680 --> 00:04:13,360
Remember that.

75
00:04:14,200 --> 00:04:15,360
Yeah, got it.

76
00:04:15,760 --> 00:04:18,620
Anyway, didn't Kanbei tell you about me?

77
00:04:18,620 --> 00:04:19,720
He did.

78
00:04:19,720 --> 00:04:24,240
You're the stupid grandson of Kanbei who came to me to learn tuna fishing,
aren't you?

79
00:04:24,240 --> 00:04:25,580
You don't need the "stupid" part.

80
00:04:25,980 --> 00:04:29,540
Now I'll teach you the
code of a man of the sea.

81
00:04:30,120 --> 00:04:33,700
A man of the sea's body is soaked
through with the scent of salt.

82
00:04:34,480 --> 00:04:37,080
Right, more than salt, you reek of booze.

83
00:04:39,020 --> 00:04:42,020
Yesterday I sailed out
onto a sea called sake.

84
00:04:42,020 --> 00:04:45,540
Whoa, as expected of a master,
that's a cool thing to say.

85
00:04:45,540 --> 00:04:47,700
There's more, so listen up.

86
00:04:47,700 --> 00:04:49,860
the place where a man of
the sea meets his end...

87
00:04:49,860 --> 00:04:50,640
Wait, hold on, hold on.

88
00:04:51,360 --> 00:04:51,760
What?

89
00:04:51,760 --> 00:04:53,900
What happened to that scar on your face?

90
00:04:53,900 --> 00:04:56,360
Did you fight a shark or something?

91
00:04:56,960 --> 00:04:57,640
This?

92
00:04:58,440 --> 00:05:01,160
I got mauled by a shark
on a hill called Neko.

93
00:05:01,160 --> 00:05:04,440
That one wasn't very cool.

94
00:05:04,440 --> 00:05:05,720
Hop on board.

95
00:05:05,720 --> 00:05:08,820
You're acting like a little kid.

96
00:05:09,640 --> 00:05:10,040
Here you go.

97
00:05:13,220 --> 00:05:14,020
Whoa!

98
00:05:14,460 --> 00:05:17,140
Why would a super-poor person
like you be in a place like this?

99
00:05:17,140 --> 00:05:18,660
That's my line!

100
00:05:21,140 --> 00:05:23,960
I see, you were moved again

101
00:05:23,960 --> 00:05:24,560
Gulp!

102
00:05:24,560 --> 00:05:26,760
N-no, well...

103
00:05:27,300 --> 00:05:29,080
Looks like I hit the nail on the head.

104
00:05:29,080 --> 00:05:29,840
Shut up!

105
00:05:30,500 --> 00:05:32,580
To become super rich,

106
00:05:32,580 --> 00:05:36,660
Papa says you need a sea
man's patience and toughness.

107
00:05:36,660 --> 00:05:38,980
I only came to train
because I have no choice.

108
00:05:38,980 --> 00:05:41,580
A city-bred rich kid like you

109
00:05:42,020 --> 00:05:43,360
will never catch a tuna.

110
00:05:43,360 --> 00:05:44,280
Shut up!

111
00:05:44,560 --> 00:05:48,580
If you catch one with your own strength,
it's promised you'll be moved.

112
00:05:49,080 --> 00:05:52,320
So you're impressed after all, aren't you?

113
00:05:53,480 --> 00:05:55,040
Shut up, you super-poor pauper!

114
00:05:55,740 --> 00:05:58,340
Being around you only brings bad luck.

115
00:05:58,340 --> 00:06:00,580
I'll train on a different boat.

116
00:06:01,960 --> 00:06:03,000
Santiago!

117
00:06:05,720 --> 00:06:06,440
Sanchaa!

118
00:06:06,440 --> 00:06:09,420
Everyone, you brought us lunch?

119
00:06:10,220 --> 00:06:12,280
I made three portions, just like you asked.

120
00:06:13,600 --> 00:06:15,740
Who are these young ladies?

121
00:06:16,440 --> 00:06:18,280
They're my girlfriends.

122
00:06:18,280 --> 00:06:19,680
Girlfriends?

123
00:06:20,300 --> 00:06:22,120
You're just like that old geezer Kanbei.

124
00:06:22,120 --> 00:06:26,360
Shouldn't a cute granddaughter
be the one bringing bento boxes?

125
00:06:26,360 --> 00:06:28,880
Men of the sea are very popular, you know.

126
00:06:28,880 --> 00:06:32,960
You must be the skinny boy
San-chan was talking about.

127
00:06:32,960 --> 00:06:34,460
B-boy?

128
00:06:34,700 --> 00:06:36,480
Make sure you catch a big tuna.

129
00:06:37,040 --> 00:06:37,400
Please.

130
00:06:37,400 --> 00:06:38,320
Huge!

131
00:06:40,260 --> 00:06:41,640
Aaaaaah!

132
00:06:43,120 --> 00:06:45,020
Leave it to me.

133
00:06:47,000 --> 00:06:49,120
What, you're coming along too?

134
00:06:53,560 --> 00:06:55,400
Alright, we're setting sail!

135
00:06:55,400 --> 00:06:57,200
Boy, cast off the rope!

136
00:06:57,200 --> 00:06:59,080
Boy!

137
00:06:59,080 --> 00:07:00,900
Come on, you idiot grandson!

138
00:07:00,900 --> 00:07:03,600
Hm? Are you talking to me?

139
00:07:03,900 --> 00:07:05,940
Why am I a "boy" too?

140
00:07:07,400 --> 00:07:12,900
Hey, in *The Old Man and the Sea*,
there's a boy who looks up to the old man!

141
00:07:12,900 --> 00:07:16,960
Not that again! Just get on with it, boy!

142
00:07:16,960 --> 00:07:18,240
Yeah, yeah, sure.

143
00:07:19,520 --> 00:07:21,700
Santiago, do your best!

144
00:07:22,120 --> 00:07:25,360
If you catch a big one,
we want a designer bag, okay?

145
00:07:33,960 --> 00:07:36,000
Is something this real
really going to be okay?

146
00:07:36,000 --> 00:07:39,040
Before we even catch any tuna,
the waves are going to swallow us whole!

147
00:07:43,420 --> 00:07:44,220
Are you okay?

148
00:07:44,220 --> 00:07:46,380
I feel sick.

149
00:07:47,180 --> 00:07:48,500
Look at you, what a pathetic sight.

150
00:07:48,500 --> 00:07:50,120
Just puke already, you squid!

151
00:07:50,660 --> 00:07:53,140
Hey boy, you're not affected at all?

152
00:07:53,140 --> 00:07:55,840
This little bit of motion doesn't bother me.

153
00:07:56,000 --> 00:07:56,983
Heh heh heh heh,

154
00:07:57,033 --> 00:08:00,480
You've got some real promise after all, boy.

155
00:08:07,360 --> 00:08:09,940
Mmmmmmmmmm?

156
00:08:10,840 --> 00:08:13,600
Hey, boy over there,
aren't you going to eat?

157
00:08:16,320 --> 00:08:19,660
What a waste. Alright, I'll eat it myself.

158
00:08:23,760 --> 00:08:24,560
Captain Santiago,

159
00:08:24,610 --> 00:08:28,180
why are so many birds gathering over there?

160
00:08:28,820 --> 00:08:31,740
Yes, let me tell you a good story.

161
00:08:32,320 --> 00:08:35,030
When birds flock over the vast ocean,

162
00:08:35,080 --> 00:08:36,920
a legendary fish appears.

163
00:08:38,540 --> 00:08:39,655
It's coming,

164
00:08:39,705 --> 00:08:42,620
the one I've been chasing all my life...

165
00:08:43,120 --> 00:08:44,860
He's about to appear!

166
00:08:56,580 --> 00:08:59,700
She may look like a wreck,
but she's got twin turbos.

167
00:08:59,700 --> 00:09:01,360
Faster than any boat out there.

168
00:09:09,180 --> 00:09:11,520
Boy, get your breath ready.

169
00:09:24,740 --> 00:09:27,240
Looks like we've struck a big tuna

170
00:09:27,240 --> 00:09:30,160
How do you even know it's a tuna?

171
00:09:30,780 --> 00:09:32,600
It's an old fisherman's instinct.

172
00:09:34,020 --> 00:09:35,860
I was watching the fish finder.

173
00:09:35,860 --> 00:09:38,780
My gut told me we should take a look.

174
00:09:38,780 --> 00:09:40,020
Hand over the squid.

175
00:09:41,520 --> 00:09:43,060
Here you go.

176
00:10:08,660 --> 00:10:10,960
Whoa! It was almost two meters!

177
00:10:10,960 --> 00:10:13,600
Isn't it an Aragami?

178
00:10:17,440 --> 00:10:20,440
You don't look happy at all
about catching a big one like this.

179
00:10:21,520 --> 00:10:24,460
This small fry isn't what I wanted to catch.

180
00:10:24,460 --> 00:10:25,820
It's an Aragami!

181
00:10:25,820 --> 00:10:27,280
Aragami?

182
00:10:27,640 --> 00:10:29,540
The lord of these waters.

183
00:10:32,280 --> 00:10:33,180
Yes!

184
00:10:41,020 --> 00:10:42,100
What, a dud?

185
00:10:42,100 --> 00:10:44,500
Isn't it a black tuna?

186
00:10:44,740 --> 00:10:45,960
It's its child.

187
00:10:45,960 --> 00:10:47,860
But a tuna is still a tuna.

188
00:10:47,860 --> 00:10:49,840
I'm definitely reeling it in!

189
00:10:59,180 --> 00:11:01,000
What was that? It was like a whale.

190
00:11:01,000 --> 00:11:03,340
Could that just now have been the Aragami?

191
00:11:06,440 --> 00:11:09,420
I never thought it really existed.

192
00:11:11,020 --> 00:11:13,780
Weren't you chasing its habits?

193
00:11:13,780 --> 00:11:15,320
Well, it's The Old Man and the Sea.

194
00:11:21,960 --> 00:11:23,040
Help me!

195
00:11:27,660 --> 00:11:29,140
Hand that over to me.

196
00:11:45,860 --> 00:11:47,340
You Aragami bastard!

197
00:11:49,900 --> 00:11:52,340
Just like I'd expect from my
rival in this final battle.

198
00:11:52,340 --> 00:11:55,260
I'll let you off the hook for today.

199
00:12:00,380 --> 00:12:01,900
It weighs 250 kilos!

200
00:12:01,900 --> 00:12:04,100
How much is it worth?

201
00:12:04,680 --> 00:12:06,140
It's worth at least five million.

202
00:12:06,140 --> 00:12:07,640
It's worth that much?

203
00:12:08,140 --> 00:12:10,700
Will catching just one
wipe out all my debts?

204
00:12:11,820 --> 00:12:17,460
Not enough visuals Kid, I'll give this tuna to you guys.
What, for real?

205
00:12:17,840 --> 00:12:27,980
I'm going to say something cool, so listen carefully.
I'm not interested in anything but Aragami. How about that? Pretty good, right?

206
00:12:29,880 --> 00:12:31,420
This is what a man of the sea is.

207
00:12:31,420 --> 00:12:33,240
Well, eheheheh.

208
00:12:36,420 --> 00:12:40,720
Super-poor kid, sorry,
but could you press the shutter for me?

209
00:12:40,720 --> 00:12:45,840
Mm. Come on, hurry up.

210
00:12:54,580 --> 00:12:58,720
That's enough for 500 people.
It's top-grade tuna.

211
00:12:59,400 --> 00:13:02,460
I had Nakagawa arrange airfreight,
so it's fresh, right?

212
00:13:02,460 --> 00:13:04,720
Apparently it sold for five million yen.

213
00:13:04,720 --> 00:13:07,740
Here, a check is fine, right?

214
00:13:13,220 --> 00:13:14,900
Amazing! This is going to make a fortune!

215
00:13:30,100 --> 00:13:35,000
Let me see, Captain Santiago's
house should be around here.

216
00:13:35,000 --> 00:13:36,140
What?

217
00:13:37,480 --> 00:13:40,200
Is that Captain Santiago's house?

218
00:13:41,240 --> 00:13:44,200
Sanchan, the boy's here!

219
00:13:45,680 --> 00:13:48,100
The boy? What's going on?

220
00:13:48,100 --> 00:13:50,680
So you're really rolling in money.

221
00:13:51,160 --> 00:13:55,720
Well, it's the result of
catching tuna since I was ten.

222
00:13:55,720 --> 00:13:57,040
Well, have a seat.

223
00:13:58,720 --> 00:14:02,792
Drinking brandy in broad daylight
with gals hanging all over you,

224
00:14:02,842 --> 00:14:03,980
what an old geezer.

225
00:14:04,560 --> 00:14:06,840
Doesn't your family complain?

226
00:14:07,680 --> 00:14:10,182
Sea men don't need families.

227
00:14:10,232 --> 00:14:12,360
I'm a lonely sea man.

228
00:14:13,740 --> 00:14:15,930
Yeah, right.
You've got women all over the place,

229
00:14:15,980 --> 00:14:18,220
and you got dumped and kicked out anyway.

230
00:14:18,960 --> 00:14:20,580
Hey, you're drunk.

231
00:14:20,900 --> 00:14:23,880
Geez, you're just like Kanbei.

232
00:14:26,020 --> 00:14:27,760
So, what do you want from me?

233
00:14:28,720 --> 00:14:30,011
I've quit the police force,

234
00:14:30,061 --> 00:14:32,880
and I've decided to become
a proper tuna fisherman.

235
00:14:33,180 --> 00:14:36,280
Please let me catch tuna with you.
I'm begging you.

236
00:14:37,280 --> 00:14:40,160
Right now, I'm only interested in Aragami.

237
00:14:41,040 --> 00:14:44,960
Aragami has already ridden the Oyashio
current off toward the Sanriku coast.

238
00:14:45,880 --> 00:14:47,580
It won't be back until next year.

239
00:14:48,000 --> 00:14:49,885
Then let's go after it.

240
00:14:49,935 --> 00:14:52,020
Let's catch Aragami, just the two of us.

241
00:14:53,240 --> 00:14:54,360
I can't.

242
00:15:10,700 --> 00:15:12,960
Shiratori, what do you think you're doing?

243
00:15:12,960 --> 00:15:17,320
Thanks to the photo you took,
Papa's misunderstanding was cleared up.

244
00:15:17,320 --> 00:15:21,020
And on top of that, look at what I am now.

245
00:15:22,620 --> 00:15:25,760
Shiratori Fisheries, President and CEO.

246
00:15:27,940 --> 00:15:31,560
When I told Papa that tuna fishing makes good money,
he lent me the funds.

247
00:15:32,140 --> 00:15:34,060
I founded a fishing company.

248
00:15:34,600 --> 00:15:36,360
How about that, you super-poor folks?

249
00:15:36,360 --> 00:15:37,940
Why don't you join my company as employees?

250
00:15:37,940 --> 00:15:41,900
Hey, San-chan, boy,
what makes us super-poor?

251
00:15:42,680 --> 00:15:45,120
Can't you see this mansion of
San-chan's right in front of you?

252
00:15:46,140 --> 00:15:47,740
It's more impressive than my family's place.

253
00:15:49,600 --> 00:15:52,800
A fine house is one thing, but with that rickety old fishing boat,
your ambitions are plain to see.

254
00:15:52,800 --> 00:15:57,140
My company has a large fishing vessel
that can sail to the ends of the earth!

255
00:16:01,900 --> 00:16:06,180
By now they're probably off Sanriku,
dropping lines after the tuna school.

256
00:16:07,260 --> 00:16:09,580
I'm planning to join them
by helicopter from here.

257
00:16:09,980 --> 00:16:13,040
Is that so?
Then take us along too, will you?

258
00:16:13,040 --> 00:16:15,840
So you want to become a
regular employee at my company?

259
00:16:15,840 --> 00:16:19,800
No, I'm saying we'll sell
you the tuna we catch, cheap.

260
00:16:19,800 --> 00:16:21,740
Captain Santiago, you're coming too, right?

261
00:16:23,580 --> 00:16:24,320
No way.

262
00:16:24,320 --> 00:16:26,300
We could catch Aragami, you know.

263
00:16:26,940 --> 00:16:30,780
Don't tell me you're scared
because Aragami is too huge?

264
00:16:31,460 --> 00:16:32,500
That's not true at all.

265
00:16:32,500 --> 00:16:33,760
Alright, it's settled.

266
00:16:34,320 --> 00:16:36,880
Then take Shiratori along, boat and all.

267
00:16:36,880 --> 00:16:37,860
Boat and all?

268
00:16:51,140 --> 00:16:53,300
It's like an elephant and an ant.

269
00:16:53,740 --> 00:16:56,940
Coastal tuna fishing isn't
worth the cost of the boat.

270
00:16:56,940 --> 00:17:00,580
What matters is speed,
getting into the school quickly.

271
00:17:00,580 --> 00:17:04,140
Stop being impressed and look for the
bird flocks like you did the other day.

272
00:17:04,660 --> 00:17:08,220
Wouldn't it be faster to search with
the fish finder than with your eyes?

273
00:17:09,420 --> 00:17:10,900
Well, I suppose that's true.

274
00:17:17,380 --> 00:17:19,400
There's a reading on it!

275
00:17:19,400 --> 00:17:20,700
Alright!

276
00:17:31,300 --> 00:17:33,020
Looks like they've spotted the tuna.

277
00:17:33,020 --> 00:17:34,720
Chase that boat!

278
00:17:40,400 --> 00:17:41,420
What are you doing?

279
00:17:41,420 --> 00:17:42,780
We're falling further and further behind!

280
00:17:43,240 --> 00:17:44,680
Boss, we can't do it!

281
00:17:44,680 --> 00:17:46,960
We're hauling the lines as hard as we can,
but it's not enough!

282
00:17:46,960 --> 00:17:48,600
That boat is way too fast!

283
00:17:54,220 --> 00:17:58,780
What a huge number of tuna! I've never
seen a school this big in the open sea.

284
00:17:59,280 --> 00:17:59,900
Whoa...

285
00:18:00,900 --> 00:18:01,560
Aaaaaah!

286
00:18:01,560 --> 00:18:03,280
Aaaaaah!

287
00:18:23,280 --> 00:18:24,860
What a bunch of monsters!

288
00:18:25,720 --> 00:18:27,660
At this rate, the boat's going to sink!

289
00:18:33,300 --> 00:18:36,660
You said 200 fish, so roughly estimating,
that's a billion yen?

290
00:18:37,240 --> 00:18:39,840
Shiratori,
I'm counting on you to pay in cash.

291
00:18:40,380 --> 00:18:42,940
Payment comes after we
sell them off monthly.

292
00:18:42,940 --> 00:18:46,040
Don't joke around!
If you don't pay here, we won't sell.

293
00:18:46,440 --> 00:18:50,060
There's no way you can come up with a billion yen right now,
you know!

294
00:18:50,060 --> 00:18:51,260
Whoa!

295
00:18:51,260 --> 00:18:51,660
Aaaaaah!

296
00:18:51,660 --> 00:18:54,640
Aaaaaah!

297
00:18:56,520 --> 00:18:57,700
Help me!

298
00:18:58,100 --> 00:18:59,540
I can't swim!

299
00:19:00,040 --> 00:19:01,000
Honestly.

300
00:19:01,000 --> 00:19:02,720
What a handful you are.

301
00:19:02,720 --> 00:19:03,180
Here, grab on.

302
00:19:19,980 --> 00:19:21,320
It's the Aragami!

303
00:19:25,420 --> 00:19:26,700
Captain Santiago!

304
00:19:26,700 --> 00:19:28,320
What are you spacing out for?

305
00:19:28,320 --> 00:19:29,700
We're hooking the Aragami!

306
00:19:30,560 --> 00:19:31,500
Impossible.

307
00:19:35,360 --> 00:19:36,780
What stubbornness!

308
00:19:39,800 --> 00:19:41,340
It's dragging the boat!

309
00:19:44,260 --> 00:19:46,160
Uh-oh, we're running out of rope!

310
00:19:46,160 --> 00:19:47,380
Captain Santiago!

311
00:19:47,380 --> 00:19:49,160
Now's not the time to be babbling!

312
00:19:49,880 --> 00:19:51,880
We're still men of the sea, damn it!

313
00:19:51,880 --> 00:19:53,980
Hemingway's weeping in his grave.

314
00:19:53,980 --> 00:19:56,700
Then you do it!

315
00:19:56,700 --> 00:19:57,100
What?

316
00:19:58,380 --> 00:20:01,700
Then you do it!

317
00:20:03,180 --> 00:20:07,540
Then just fight like Rocky!

318
00:20:07,660 --> 00:20:09,260
Let me down, you!

319
00:20:12,070 --> 00:20:12,840
Idiot!

320
00:20:13,620 --> 00:20:16,400
Whoa! No way!

321
00:20:18,880 --> 00:20:20,300
Ugh, whoa!

322
00:20:20,480 --> 00:20:24,762
Ugh... easy, easy,

323
00:20:24,812 --> 00:20:34,200
Now it's do or die!

324
00:21:10,180 --> 00:21:13,240
My rival,
what a magnificent battle that was.

325
00:21:13,820 --> 00:21:17,700
Sea man Santiago has finally hooked Aragami!

326
00:21:18,060 --> 00:21:19,420
Ahahahaha!

327
00:21:19,420 --> 00:21:22,560
Don't mess with me! You didn't do anything!

328
00:21:24,000 --> 00:21:25,160
Whoaaaaa!

329
00:21:25,280 --> 00:21:26,300
Aaaaaaah!

330
00:21:27,800 --> 00:21:31,540
Whoa! Help me! I can't swim!

331
00:21:32,340 --> 00:21:35,040
What kind of sea man can't swim?

332
00:21:38,840 --> 00:21:41,320
Captain Santiago was really pleased

333
00:21:45,400 --> 00:21:48,900
One tuna worth a hundred million,
that was some amazing tuna.

334
00:21:51,500 --> 00:21:53,940
We just got onto the
Metropolitan Expressway.

335
00:21:54,480 --> 00:21:56,120
About twenty more minutes, I think.

336
00:21:57,580 --> 00:22:00,880
Then everyone's waiting with
their necks stretched out.

337
00:22:00,880 --> 00:22:02,420
I'd imagine so.

338
00:22:02,420 --> 00:22:05,600
Because that's 200 golden
bluefin tuna at once.

339
00:22:06,920 --> 00:22:08,060
By the way, Shiratori.

340
00:22:08,060 --> 00:22:09,680
As for my share,

341
00:22:09,680 --> 00:22:11,560
eight should be fine, right?

342
00:22:11,560 --> 00:22:13,180
What are you talking about?

343
00:22:13,180 --> 00:22:15,540
Obviously I get eight and you get two.

344
00:22:15,540 --> 00:22:18,340
We're the ones paying for all the transport costs,
after all.

345
00:22:19,060 --> 00:22:19,940
That's how it is.

346
00:22:21,300 --> 00:22:22,180
Wait!

347
00:22:22,180 --> 00:22:23,920
Look ahead!

348
00:22:26,320 --> 00:22:27,200
Shit!

349
00:22:39,000 --> 00:22:42,540
You're the one who said something stupid,
and now look what's happened!

350
00:22:42,540 --> 00:22:44,580
Isn't it because you got greedy?

351
00:22:53,180 --> 00:22:54,080
This is bad!

352
00:22:54,080 --> 00:22:56,040
A single tuna worth five million yen...

353
00:22:56,040 --> 00:22:57,600
We've gotta catch Shiratori!

354
00:22:59,180 --> 00:22:59,900
Damn it!

355
00:22:59,900 --> 00:23:00,480
Bwaun!

356
00:23:05,680 --> 00:23:06,540
The tuna!

357
00:23:12,040 --> 00:23:14,080
Come on, it's not stopping at all!

358
00:23:16,840 --> 00:23:17,200
What?

359
00:23:35,620 --> 00:23:37,800
Papa's going to be impressed again.

360
00:23:37,800 --> 00:23:40,380
My one billion yen...

361
00:24:01,080 --> 00:24:04,560
Sandals any time, scandals any time,
don't mind a thing.

362
00:24:05,380 --> 00:24:08,400
Playing "Kuudel" every day.

363
00:24:08,400 --> 00:24:13,960
Boredom? I crumpled it into
a reprimand and tossed it away.

364
00:24:15,060 --> 00:24:18,500
Bare instincts, naked instincts,
going wild and dumb.

365
00:24:19,540 --> 00:24:22,280
Reckless and broke, so what?

366
00:24:23,900 --> 00:24:29,040
My way, doing whatever I want,
I just do it and won't let myself rot.

367
00:24:31,420 --> 00:24:35,580
Smoke from my head,
run away and you'll end up in Kameari.

368
00:24:35,580 --> 00:24:38,240
Well, how wonderful! Oho!

369
00:24:38,240 --> 00:24:40,320
In the flowery Edo, Joito!

370
00:24:40,320 --> 00:24:42,860
Ryozan typhoon, as always.

371
00:24:42,860 --> 00:24:44,900
Raging wild.

372
00:24:45,480 --> 00:24:47,320
We work hard, yeah, Kyū-baiku.

373
00:24:47,320 --> 00:24:51,300
Jugemu jugemu, heart worn thin,
as easy as fish and water.

374
00:24:51,300 --> 00:24:54,680
Suigyo matsugu, gyo matsugu, rai matsugu.

375
00:24:54,680 --> 00:24:56,420
A place to sleep, a place to live.

376
00:24:56,920 --> 00:25:00,260
Yamura Kōji Burakōji,
Paipo Paipo Paipo no -

377
00:25:00,260 --> 00:25:03,080
Shūringan shūringan no Kūrintai.

378
00:25:03,080 --> 00:25:06,280
Kūrintai no Ponpoko Kī no Ponpoko nado.

379
00:25:06,280 --> 00:25:08,020
Super-investigation, rhythm series.

380
00:25:14,020 --> 00:25:16,700
Everyone,
thanks for all your help until now.

381
00:25:16,700 --> 00:25:18,500
Now it's time to say goodbye to all of you.

382
00:25:18,500 --> 00:25:21,340
Just kidding, just kidding!
Did I surprise you?

383
00:25:21,340 --> 00:25:24,020
Did you really think this leg
would just disappear that easily?

384
00:25:24,020 --> 00:25:26,640
I just wanted to give you a little scare.

385
00:25:26,640 --> 00:25:27,860
Hey, wait a minute!

386
00:25:27,860 --> 00:25:29,080
I was lying, I told you!

387
00:25:29,080 --> 00:25:31,880
Next time: Operation Goodbye, Ryo-san!

388
00:25:31,880 --> 00:25:32,960
Take care, all of you.

389
00:25:32,960 --> 00:25:35,780
Over there is Kame-ari.

390
00:25:36,700 --> 00:25:39,100
Surely it's Kame-ari.

391
00:25:40,400 --> 00:25:42,240
Come on, everyone, come over!

392
00:25:42,240 --> 00:25:44,240
To our town!

393
00:25:45,260 --> 00:25:45,860
Thank you.

